# launch-hush-planet-chapter.rish -- print the loop for HUSH, Dream's planet.
# STATUS -- elder printer, kept as testimony. The living recipe is
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/launch-fleet-chapter.rish hush
# which reads construction/fleet-roster.kyri, so a ship joins, retires, or is renamed in one row
# rather than in a printer of its own (REDS %409). This file keeps every byte it wrote -- it
# carries living and dated references both -- and it names hush in its filename beside an
# astrological MODALITY, `planet`, which named which body orbits which star. That arrangement
# changed and the filename did not, so the breach is one line: a launcher is named for its seat,
# never for its modality. Prepped Class H in construction/SHRED_PREP.md; the cut stays RED until
# Keaton circles it, and the ship name itself is not touched.
#
#
# Hush is Dream's own night twin made a working hand: the star holds the systems core as Codex
# on the pier, and its planet runs CLAUDE CODE ON THE SAME PIER in its own tree ~/grain-hush
# (moved from the Framework on Keaton's word, 20260829), working the hands-on
# systems half beside it -- POND COMPLETING THE AI-JAIL ENCLOSURE under the accrete-only
# documentation boundary, and the STANDING ADAPTATION GRANT (bash to Rishi, HTML to Brush,
# Python to Glow). A planet defers to its star where lanes brush: Pond leans on Caravan's
# capability and address-space pieces, and a change wanted inside caravan/ or tally/ is Dream's
# lane -- a line on the card. Lane seated by the role swap of 20260827.155213 on Keaton's word.
# Charter: active-designing/20260829-203718_the-six-bodies-and-the-always-fleet.md.
#
#   rishi/bin/rishi run tools/l/launch-hush-planet-chapter.rish

# invariant: run from the repo root, where the durable memory lives.
let root = run ["test" "-f" "construction/ITINERARY.md"]
assert root.ok else "run from the repo root (construction/ITINERARY.md not found)"

# invariant: the living charter this seat lives in must exist.
let charter = run ["test" "-f" "active-designing/20260829-203718_the-six-bodies-and-the-always-fleet.md"]
assert charter.ok else "the six-bodies charter is missing"

say "HUSH -- Dream's planet (the star's own night twin, made a hand)"
say "==============================================================="
say ""
say "Host: CLAUDE CODE ON THE VULTR PIER, a terminal loop in its own tree"
say "~/grain-hush beside Dream's ~/grain-dream. The shared discipline lives on"
say "the living card; the lane lives in the six-bodies charter; both are read"
say "fresh every lap."
say ""
say "0) PRECONDITIONS, once per machine: this repo cloned with the xy remote;"
say "   git submodule update --init --recursive; jq for the readable stream"
say "   (the distribution package, or drop the jq tail and raw NDJSON scrolls)."
say "   Power is a preference, never a gate: the repo is the durable memory, a"
say "   cut lap costs only its uncommitted work, the next round-open pull"
say "   resumes the thread."
say ""
say "1) BYPASS STANDING (once, gitignored): in .claude/settings.local.json set"
say "   permissions.defaultMode = bypassPermissions -- or keep the flag below."
say "   Claude refuses the flag as root; run as a plain user."
say ""
say "2) SMOKE TEST:"
say "   claude --dangerously-skip-permissions --effort max -p 'reply with exactly: pong'"
say ""

say "3) THE SEAT PROMPT is a file, tools/h/hush_seat_prompt.txt -- never a shell"
say "   string: an apostrophe inside a single-quoted one-liner strands the shell"
say "   at its continuation prompt (Silence hit it first, 20260829)."
say ""
say "   ONE ROUND, ONCE:"
say ""
say "LOOP_LAPS=1 sh tools/f/fleet-loop.sh hush"
say ""
say "4) THE LOOP -- anchored to the tree that holds the script; LOOP_HOURS bounds"
say "   it (default 18), epoch arithmetic so one spelling fits both benches:"
say ""
say "sh tools/f/fleet-loop.sh hush"
say ""
say "5) STREAMING: the loop tees the raw stream to session-output/hush.jsonl and"
say "   the rendered turns to session-output/hush.txt, inside the tree."
say ""
say "6) WHY A FILE SENTINEL: stream-json echoes the prompt, which contains the"
say "   words GATES-ONLY, so a grep on the stream would false-stop after one lap."
say ""
say "7) CUSTODY: the gates in ITINERARY stay MANUAL -- funds and keys, provisioning"
say "   and paying, the maintainer's own identity, and the public seed."
say ""
say "MANY HANDS (granted 20260828, Keaton's word): this seat may spin up multiple"
say "CLI agents and manage them -- subagents, worker sessions, parallel claude or"
say "codex dependents -- when dividing a lap pays. Every standing law rides into"
say "each dependent: custody gates stay MANUAL, one writer per checkout (the %291"
say "habit -- ListAgents, name the peer, precise-stage whole-index commits, %376), and the parent"
say "seat answers for what its dependents stage."
say ""
say "GREEN: Hush recipe printed -- the star holds the core, and its planet closes the enclosure around it."
